<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="zh-Hant">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Day {{ '%02d' % day }} · {{ theme_en }}</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #f6f5f2; --card: #fff; --ink: #1a1a1a; --ink-soft: #6b6b6b;
    --accent: #2a7a4f; --accent-soft: #e5f0ea;
    --dict: #1f6f78; --read: #4a6fa5; --ref: #7a5aa3; --pat: #8a6a2f;
    --flow: #a35a5a;
    --border: #e4e0d8; --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.03), 0 6px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.05);
    --mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Monaco, monospace;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "PingFang TC", "Noto Sans TC", sans-serif;
    background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;
    -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 18px 60px; }
  .top { background: #fff; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .top .inner { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 11px 18px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; }
  .top .brand { font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; }
  .top .brand small { color: var(--ink-soft); font-weight: 400; margin-left: 6px; }
  .top .up { margin-left: auto; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-soft); text-decoration: none; }

  .hero { padding: 30px 0 6px; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 27px; margin: 0 0 4px; }
  .hero p { color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; font-size: 14px; }
  .today { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .today .m { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 13px; text-align: center; }
  .today .m b { display: block; font-size: 24px; font-family: var(--mono); }
  .today .m span { font-size: 10.5px; color: var(--ink-soft); letter-spacing: .5px; text-transform: uppercase; }

  h2.sec { font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 1.4px; color: var(--ink-soft); text-transform: uppercase;
           margin: 30px 0 12px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
  h2.sec::after { content: ""; flex: 1; height: 1px; background: var(--border); }

  /* Numbered rows, not competing cards — the three pages are a sequence, and
     side-by-side cards of equal weight cannot say that. */
  .cards { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
  .c { text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink); background: #fff;
       border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 5px solid var(--tc); border-radius: 13px;
       box-shadow: var(--shadow); padding: 15px 16px;
       display: grid; grid-template-columns: 30px 1fr auto; gap: 4px 13px; align-items: center; }
  .c[aria-disabled] { opacity: .45; pointer-events: none; }
  .c .n { grid-area: 1 / 1 / 3 / 2; align-self: start; margin-top: 2px;
          width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%; background: #f2f0ec; color: var(--ink-soft);
          font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700;
          display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
  .c .nm { grid-area: 1 / 2 / 2 / 3; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 700; }
  .c .nm .ic { margin-right: 7px; }
  .c .cnt { grid-area: 1 / 3 / 3 / 4; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 700;
            color: var(--tc); white-space: nowrap; align-self: center; }
  .c .sub { grid-area: 2 / 2 / 3 / 3; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.5; }
  .note { font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.75; margin-top: 22px; }
  /* Time budget — the four steps do not fit an evening by accident, so the page
     says what each one costs instead of leaving it to be discovered. */
  .budget { margin-top: 26px; border: 1px solid var(--border); background: #fff;
            border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px 16px; }
  .budget h3 { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 1.2px; text-transform: uppercase;
               color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 10px; font-weight: 600; }
  .budget table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12.5px; }
  .budget td { padding: 4px 0; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .budget td.t { font-family: var(--mono); text-align: right; color: var(--ink); white-space: nowrap; }
  .budget tr.sum td { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 8px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .today { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="top"><div class="inner">
  <div class="brand">{{ day_icon|default('📘') }} Day {{ '%02d' % day }} <small>{{ theme_en }}</small></div>
  <a class="up" href="../index.html">← All days</a>
</div></div>

<div class="wrap">
  <div class="hero">
    <h1>{{ theme_en }}</h1>
    <p>Skim the words, hear them, learn the patterns, then drill. About two hours end to end.</p>
    <div class="today">
      <div class="m"><b>{{ chunks|length }}</b><span>Chunks</span></div>
      <div class="m"><b>{{ n_supp }}</b><span>Extra words</span></div>
      <div class="m"><b>{{ stories|default([])|length }}</b><span>Stories</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="sec">Today, in order</h2>
  <div class="cards">
    <a class="c" style="--tc:var(--ref)" href="reference.html"{% if not has_supp %} aria-disabled="true"{% endif %}>
      <span class="n">1</span>
      <span class="nm"><span class="ic">📚</span>Word List</span>
      <span class="cnt">{% if has_supp %}{{ n_supp }} words →{% else %}not built{% endif %}</span>
      <span class="sub">Skim, do not memorize. One pass to see what today is made of, so the drills
      later land on something you have already met. Concept diagrams are worth stopping on; the bare
      English&nbsp;→&nbsp;Chinese pairs are not.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="c" style="--tc:var(--flow)" href="player.html"{% if not has_player %} aria-disabled="true"{% endif %}>
      <span class="n">·</span>
      <span class="nm"><span class="ic">🔁</span>Vocab Flow</span>
      <span class="cnt">{% if has_player %}{{ chunks|length + n_supp }} cards →{% else %}not built{% endif %}</span>
      <span class="sub">Hands-free playback for the words themselves. Each card shows the word, reads it
      in both voices, pauses for you to say it, then gives the Chinese and the example sentence. High
      frequency first, extra vocab after. Put it on while your hands are busy — it is the one step that
      does not need you at the keyboard.{% if not has_player %} Run <b>build_vocab_flow.py</b> for this
      day to generate it.{% endif %}</span>
    </a>
    <a class="c" style="--tc:var(--pat)" href="chunks.html"{% if not has_chunks_page %} aria-disabled="true"{% endif %}>
      <span class="n">·</span>
      <span class="nm"><span class="ic">🎯</span>Core Chunks</span>
      <span class="cnt">{% if has_chunks_page %}{{ chunks|length }} chunks →{% else %}not built{% endif %}</span>
      <span class="sub">Reference, not a step — the day's own {{ chunks|length }} high-frequency
      expressions with the scene, the word family and the pattern for each. Practice shows these one
      answer at a time; this is where you can go back and read them. Marks which ones you have missed
      in the drills.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="c" style="--tc:var(--read)" href="story.html"{% if not has_story %} aria-disabled="true"{% endif %}>
      <span class="n">2</span>
      <span class="nm"><span class="ic">🎬</span>Story Player</span>
      <span class="cnt">{% if has_story %}{{ stories|default([])|length }} stories →{% else %}not built{% endif %}</span>
      <span class="sub">Sentence-by-sentence playback with speed control. For shadowing and for warming
      up, not for testing — the transcript is on screen the whole time.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="c" style="--tc:var(--pat)" href="patterns.html"{% if not has_patterns %} aria-disabled="true"{% endif %}>
      <span class="n">3</span>
      <span class="nm"><span class="ic">🧩</span>Pattern Network</span>
      <span class="cnt">{% if has_patterns %}6 families →{% else %}not built{% endif %}</span>
      <span class="sub">The prepositions, the word families and the transitive traps, grouped by the
      rule that generates them rather than by word. Each family ends in Part 5 drills; the full pattern
      table stays locked until you have answered them.{% if not has_patterns %} Hand-authored so far —
      only Day 02 has one.{% endif %}</span>
    </a>
    <a class="c" style="--tc:var(--dict)" href="practice.html"{% if not has_practice %} aria-disabled="true"{% endif %}>
      <span class="n">4</span>
      <span class="nm"><span class="ic">🎧</span>Practice</span>
      <span class="cnt">{% if has_practice %}6 steps →{% else %}not built{% endif %}</span>
      <span class="sub">Where the day actually happens. Vocabulary and Chunk Drill first, then Reading
      Speed, then the same material by ear — Chunk Dictation and Story Listening, both with the text
      withheld until you have answered. Ends on the Transfer Test.{% if not has_practice %} Run
      <b>build_trr.py</b> for this day to generate it.{% endif %}</span>
    </a>
    <a class="c" style="--tc:var(--ref)" href="reading.html"{% if not has_reading %} aria-disabled="true"{% endif %}>
      <span class="n">5</span>
      <span class="nm"><span class="ic">📄</span>Reading Test</span>
      <span class="cnt">{% if has_reading %}36 items →{% else %}not built{% endif %}</span>
      <span class="sub">Parts 5, 6 and 7 mixed and unlabelled, over four passage sets built from today's
      words — every chunk and every supplementary word appears. Read each set once before the questions
      open, and the reading rate is recorded. Nothing is marked until you submit a set; then that set
      opens in full, with all four options translated and a reason each one lives or dies, beside the
      passage in Chinese.{% if not has_reading %} Run <b>build_reading.py</b> for this day to generate
      it.{% endif %}</span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="budget">
    <h3>What the four steps cost</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><td>1 · Word List — one skim, not end to end</td><td class="t">~10 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>· &nbsp;Vocab Flow — hands-free, runs alongside anything</td><td class="t">~55 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2 · Story Player</td><td class="t">~10 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>3 · Pattern Network</td><td class="t">~25 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>4 · Practice</td><td class="t">~73 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>5 · Reading Test — 4 sets, 36 items, review after each set</td><td class="t">~26 min</td></tr>
      <tr class="sum"><td>Full sequence</td><td class="t">~144 min</td></tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="note">
    <b>Steps 1 and 3 are the ones to cut when the evening is short.</b> Practice is the only step that
    tests speed under time pressure, and the Story Player is the only one that trains the ear — those
    two are the floor. Reading the Word List end to end costs roughly 25 minutes on its own and buys
    vocabulary-test confidence rather than listening, which is why step 1 is a skim.
  </p>
  <p class="note">
    The Listen / Meaning / Cloze drills that used to live on this page were removed on 2026-08-07.
    Meaning ran English&nbsp;→&nbsp;Chinese, which trained the translation loop this project exists to
    break; Listen and Cloze were folded into <b>Chunk Dictation</b>, where one item now does the work all
    three used to — hear the sentence, then rebuild the chunk from word tiles.
  </p>
</div>

</body>
</html>
